{"strongs": "H1389", "word": "גִּבְעָה", "translit": "giv.ah", "root": "גבע", "morph": "H:N-F", "pos": "noun feminine", "gloss": "hill", "definition": "I. גִּבְעָה noun feminine hill — absolute גִּבְעָה 2Sam 2:25 + 13 t. + Ezek 6:13 (strike out Co q. v.) 1Sam 7:1 ; 2Sam 6:3 ; 2Sam 6:4 (compare Dr ); construct גִּבְעַת Josh 5:3 + 8 t. + 1Sam 10:5 (compare Dr ); suffix גִּבְעָתִי Ezek 34:26 (but strike out Co ), גִּבְעָתָהּ Isa 31:4 plural absolute גְּבָעוֺת Deut 12:2 + 35 t.; construct גִּבְעוֺת Deut 33:15 ; Hab 3:6 , גִּבְעֹת Gen 49:26 suffix גִּבְעוֺתֶיךָ Ezek 35:8 — hill, height, elevation , both high and low, compare Ps 148:9 ההרים וכל גבעות , Ps 65:13 — 1. in ordinary prose, hill , lower than mountain Exod 17:9 ; Exod 17:10 ( E ) 2Sam 2:25 it may be proper name in 1Sam 7:1 ; 1Sam 10:10 ; 2Sam 6:3 ; 2Sam 6:4 see also below II. גִּבְעָה . 2. especially as place of illicit worship גְּבֹהָה ותחת כל עץ רענן ׳ עַל כָּלגֿ 1Kgs 14:23 ; 2Kgs 17:10 ; Jer 2:20 compare Deut 12:2 ; 2Kgs 16:4 ; 2Chr 28:4 (these two + במות ); also Hos 4:13 ; Jer 13:27 ; Jer 17:2 ; Ezek 6:13 (see above). 3. very commonly || הר in poetry & prophets Deut 33:15 ; Ps 72:3 ; Ps 114:4 ; Ps 114:6 ; Ps 148:9 ; Song 2:8 ; Song 4:6 ; Isa 2:2 ; Isa 2:14 ; Isa 30:17 ; Isa 30:25 ; Isa 31:4 ; Isa 40:4 ; Isa 40:12 ; Isa 41:15 ; Isa 42:15 ; Isa 54:10 ; Isa 55:12 ; Isa 65:7 ; Jer 3:23 ; Jer 4:24 ; Jer 16:16 ; Jer 50:7 ; Ezek 6:3 ; Ezek 34:6 ; Ezek 35:8 ; Ezek 36:4 ; Ezek 36:6 ; Hos 4:13 ; Hos 10:8 ; Josh 4:18 ; Amos 9:13 ; Mic 4:1 ; Mic 6:1 ; Nah 1:5 ; Hab 3:6 rarely in prose Deut 12:2 sometimes as high and majestic (poetry) עולם ׳ ג Gen 49:26 ; Deut 33:15 ; Hab 3:6 ('everlasting hills'); compare also Job 15:7 ; Prov 8:25 (with adjective high , compare above); see also Jer 49:16 . 4. hills with special names, some nearly or quite = proper name, of a location, which see under the respective words: מֹרֶה ׳ ג Judg 7:1 teacher's hill , in valley of Jezreel; הָעֲרָלוֺת ׳ ג Josh 5:3 hill of the fore-skins ; הָאֱלֹהִים ׳ ג 1Sam 10:5 (a designation of Gibeah); הַחֲכִילָה ׳ ג 1Sam 23:19 ; 1Sam 26:1 ; 1Sam 26:3 אַמָּה ׳ ג 2Sam 2:24 הַלְּבוֺנָה ׳ ג Song 4:6 (i.e. hill where frankincense is grown); גָּרֵב֑ ׳ ג Jer 31:39 יְרוּשָׁלַם ׳ ג Isa 10:32 compare Isa 31:4 (where || הַרצִֿיּוֺן ), Ezek 34:26 (see above) & הַגְּבָעוֺת Zeph 1:10 hills on which Jerusalem stands.", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1452')\">BDB1452</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H1389')\">H1389</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1451')\">BDB1451</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1453')\">BDB1453</entry></div><p> I. <bdbheb>גִּבְעָה</bdbheb> <b>noun feminine</b> <highlightword>hill</highlightword> — absolute <bdbheb>גִּבְעָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Sam 2:25\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(10,2,25)\">2Sam 2:25</ref> + 13 t. + <ref ref=\"Ezek 6:13\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(26,6,13)\">Ezek 6:13</ref> (strike out <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Co')\">Co</lookup> q. v.) <ref ref=\"1Sam 7:1\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(9,7,1)\">1Sam 7:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 6:3\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(10,6,3)\">2Sam 6:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 6:4\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(10,6,4)\">2Sam 6:4</ref> (compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dr')\">Dr</lookup>); construct <bdbheb>גִּבְעַת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Josh 5:3\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(6,5,3)\">Josh 5:3</ref> + 8 t. + <ref ref=\"1Sam 10:5\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(9,10,5)\">1Sam 10:5</ref> (compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dr')\">Dr</lookup>); suffix <bdbheb>גִּבְעָתִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 34:26\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(26,34,26)\">Ezek 34:26</ref> (but strike out <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Co')\">Co</lookup>), <bdbheb>גִּבְעָתָהּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 31:4\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(23,31,4)\">Isa 31:4</ref> plural absolute <bdbheb>גְּבָעוֺת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 12:2\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(5,12,2)\">Deut 12:2</ref> + 35 t.; construct <bdbheb>גִּבְעוֺת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 33:15\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(5,33,15)\">Deut 33:15</ref>; <ref ref=\"Hab 3:6\" b=\"35\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(35,3,6)\">Hab 3:6</ref>, <bdbheb>גִּבְעֹת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 49:26\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"49\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"49\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(1,49,26)\">Gen 49:26</ref> suffix <bdbheb>גִּבְעוֺתֶיךָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 35:8\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"35\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"35\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(26,35,8)\">Ezek 35:8</ref> — <highlight>hill, height, elevation</highlight>, both high and low, compare <ref ref=\"Ps 148:9\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"148\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"148\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(19,148,9)\">Ps 148:9</ref> <bdbheb>ההרים וכל גבעות</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"Ps 65:13\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"65\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"65\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(19,65,13)\">Ps 65:13</ref> — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> in ordinary prose, <highlight>hill</highlight>, lower than mountain <ref ref=\"Exod 17:9\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(2,17,9)\">Exod 17:9</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 17:10\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(2,17,10)\">Exod 17:10</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>) <ref ref=\"2Sam 2:25\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(10,2,25)\">2Sam 2:25</ref> it may be proper name in <ref ref=\"1Sam 7:1\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(9,7,1)\">1Sam 7:1<